desc:M1K [analogue poly synth] (GFX Lab)
//tags: instrument synth poly analogue rack layer chorus delay
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-lab-drift, gfx-lab-output, gfx-lab-ui, gfx-lab-panel, gfx-lab-instrument, gfx-lab-voice, gfx-lab-dyn, gfx-lab-faceplate
// (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// Hybrid rework of the Stable M1K: a six-voice analogue rack module in the spirit of the late-80s matrix-modulation
// synths, that now plays TWO patches at once, layered.
// LAYER       patch A and patch B, each any of the 100 factory patches (then edited as you like), both sound on every
//             note (six voices each). LAYER B switches patch B in and out (a 20 ms fade); BALANCE mixes the two
//             (centre = both full, left = A alone, right = B alone). The A / B keys pick which patch the display,
//             the patch list and the editor show. Each patch keeps its own LEVEL and GLIDE; the PLAY settings
//             (voices, velocity, bend) and the Mod Rack are patch A's.
// VOICE       two DCOs each: a SAW that morphs to TRIANGLE (SHAPE) and a PULSE (PW), switched in independently;
//             DCO 2 adds NOISE (in place of its waves) and SYNC to DCO 1; MIX balances the two.
//             24 dB low-pass VCF: CUTOFF, RESONANCE, ENV 1 amount, KEY tracking and FM (DCO 1 sweeping the cutoff).
//             VCA 1 = velocity and level; VCA 2 = ENV 2.
//             VCF VEL: velocity opens the cutoff (up to +5 oct).
//             Two DADSR envelopes: ENV 1 -> VCF (and PITCH: DCO 2 or both, +/-24 st), ENV 2 -> VCA.
//             LFO 1 -> vibrato, with DELAY (fades in after each note); mod wheel and aftertouch add vibrato.
//             LFO 2 -> PW, CUTOFF (+/-5 oct) or PITCH (+/-12 st).
// MOD RACK    the GFX Mod Rack inside: CHORUS, TREMOLO, VIBE and DELAY, each with L / C / R outputs and tempo SYNC,
//             on both layers together, set by patch A.
// COMBI       27 factory pairs (KEYS, STRINGS, SYNTH, BASS, LEAD, MALLETS + FX): one click loads patch A and patch B
//             together, each at a matched LEVEL, BALANCE set and LAYER B in (Reaper's parameter list: Combi).
// PATCHES     100 factory patches in seven banks (KEYBOARD, STRINGS, WIND+PERC, SYNTH, BASS, LEAD, EFFECTS).
//             Choosing a patch loads every voice setting (your edits stay until you choose another patch -
//             save them as a Reaper preset).
// PLAY        POLY (6 voices), MONO (legato, last note) or UNISON (all six voices on one note, spread).
//             GLIDE, VELOCITY, BEND range, VOLUME, MIDI channel.
// DRIFT (tuning): the tuning wanders, each voice's DCOs drift apart in fine pitch, and every note lands slightly
//             differently in tune (both layers, each voice on its own).
// MIDI: pitch bend, CC1 mod wheel, channel aftertouch, CC64 sustain, CC123 all notes off; everything passes through.
// FACEPLATE   black (the early boxes) or cream (the 90s boxes): the key beside the display swaps them.
// Latency: 0 samples.

import gfx-lab-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-voice.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-dyn.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-faceplate.jsfx-inc

